# Local Cloudflare deployment credentials. Copy this file to .secrets.env,
# fill the values locally, and never commit the populated file.
#
# Use one Cloudflare API token for both OAuth KV management and Worker
# deployment. Do not create separate billing, D1, route-profile, or Access
# tokens: this project does not use those APIs.
#
# Scope the token to the target account with these permissions:
# - Account / Workers Scripts: Edit
# - Account / Workers KV Storage: Edit
# - Account / Account Settings: Read
# - Zone / Workers Routes: Edit, limited to trustedtunnel.app
#
# For a user-owned token, Wrangler identity discovery also requires:
# - User / User Details: Read
# - User / Memberships: Read
#
# No Billing, DNS, certificate, D1, R2, or Access permission is required.
# Account API Tokens: Read is useful for inspecting this token's policy during
# setup, but it is not required for deployment or runtime operation.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID selects the account. It is an identifier, not a token.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
